{"id":"rp2047-3","designation":"RP 2047-3","title":"Carriage of VC-2 Compressed Video — VC-2 Level 65 Compression of High Definition Video Sources for Use with a Standard Definition Infrastructure","state":"active","suite":"2047","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/rp2047-3/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/rp2047-3/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This Recommended Practice defines constraints on the VC-2 video compression standard such that 10-bit high-definition video signals can be compressed to only occupy the bit rate of 8-bit standard definition signals. Specifically, it defines constraints for compressing interlaced source video having 1920 or 1440 pixels/line by 1080 lines/frame at 25 or 30/1.001 frames/s, or progressive source video having 1280 pixels/line by 720 lines/frame at 50 or 60/1.001 frames/s, using 4:2:2 sampling in all cases. It also defines an application-specific level value corresponding to these constraints.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"Foreword","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Introduction","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"2 Normative references","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"3 Terms and definitions","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"4 Overview (informative)","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"5 Coding constraints","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 Summary (informative)","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 Video source parameters","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 Coding parameters","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"5.3.1 Syntax","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"5.3.2 Sequence header","page":7},{"level":4,"title":"5.3.2.1 General","page":7},{"level":4,"title":"5.3.2.2 Parse parameters","page":7},{"level":4,"title":"5.3.2.3 Base video format","page":7},{"level":4,"title":"5.3.2.4 Source parameters","page":8},{"level":4,"title":"5.3.2.5 Picture coding mode","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"5.3.3 Picture syntax","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"5.3.4 Transform parameters","page":8},{"level":4,"title"